+# Writing prompts for free-web-ai-worker
+
+This tool only carries **plain text in and plain text out**. The web AI cannot
+see your conversation, your files, or your repository — so every prompt must be
+self-contained. Everything below follows from that one constraint.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Starting a new conversation
+
+You usually do not have to think about this:
+
+- Every call opens the site root in a **fresh tab**, which is already a new chat
+  for Duck.ai, Qwen, DeepSeek and others.
+- With `defaults.newChat: true` (the default) the tool additionally clicks the
+  site's own **"New chat" control** when it can find one (`NEW_CHAT` selectors
+  in each provider). This matters for sites that restore the previous thread,
+  where a stale conversation could bleed into your answer.
+- Pass `--no-new-chat` to continue the site's current conversation instead.
+
+You do **not** need to ask the web AI to "start a new chat" — that is the
+tool's job, not the prompt's.
+
+---
+
+## 2. The shape of a good prompt (5 parts)
+
+```
+1. Instruction     "You are a careful editor."
+2. Task verb       "Summarise the text below."
+3. Input           delimited — see §4
+4. Output format   "Output exactly 3 bullet points, each under 20 words."
+5. Constraint      "Output only the bullets. No preamble, no explanation."
+```
+
+Most bad delegations are missing parts 4 and 5: the model then answers with
+"How can I help?" or three paragraphs of commentary around the one line you
+wanted.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Control the output format explicitly
+
+Be boring and literal. State the exact shape, and give a one-line example.
+
+| You want | Say this |
+|---|---|
+| Machine-readable | `Output only a JSON object with keys name, date, amount. No code fences, no explanation.` |
+| One label per line | `Output one label per line, in the same order as the input. Nothing else.` |
+| Translation only | `Output the translation only. Do not add the original text.` |
+| Strict vocabulary | `Use only the labels: bug, feature, question.` |
+| No commentary | `Do not explain your reasoning. Do not add a summary.` |
+
+If you need to parse it, say **"Output only JSON"** and strip code fences
+anyway before parsing — a model may wrap it in ```json regardless.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Delimit the input
+
+Never let the model guess where the instruction ends and the text begins.
+Wrap the payload:
+
+```bash
+ask-web-ai ask "Summarise the text between <text> tags in 3 sentences. Output only the summary.
+
+<text>
+...long article...
+</text>" -p duckai --json
+```
+
+Alternatives that work well: `---` fences, `###`, or an explicit
+`INPUT:\n...\nEND INPUT`.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Length and encoding
+
+- Prefer prompts under a few thousand characters. For anything longer, avoid
+  shell-escaping entirely and use a file or pipe:
+
+```bash
+ask-web-ai ask --file ./subtask.txt -p duckai --json
+cat notes.md | ask-web-ai ask --stdin -p duckai --json
+```
+
+- The answer is capped at `defaults.maxAnswerChars` (200k by default) and
+  `meta.truncated` tells you if it was cut.
+- **Never paste secrets.** The prompt travels to a third-party website.
+
+---
+
+## 6. State the output language
+
+The site may default to its own UI language. If you want Chinese out, say so:
+
+```
+Output in Simplified Chinese.
+```
+
+---
+
+## 7. What NOT to put in a prompt
+
+These belong on the main model — the router will tell you so:
+
+- anything needing your repository, files, or project context
+- editing files, running tests, using tools
+- multi-step work ("first do X, then based on that do Y")
+- current facts (prices, news, today's version) — the web AI will hallucinate
+- security-critical judgement
+
+Ask first:
+
+```bash
+ask-web-ai route "Summarise this article"     # -> DELEGATE
+ask-web-ai route "Refactor the auth module"   # -> KEEP
+```
+
+---
+
+## 8. Templates
+
+**Summarise**
+
+```
+Summarise the text between <text> tags in 3 sentences. Output only the summary.
+
+<text>
+{{TEXT}}
+</text>
+```
+
+**Classify a batch**
+
+```
+Classify each line as bug / feature / question.
+Output one label per line, in the same order as the input. Nothing else.
+
+{{LINES}}
+```
+
+**Extract to JSON**
+
+```
+Extract name, date and amount from the text between <text> tags.
+Output only a JSON object with keys name, date, amount. No code fences.
+
+<text>
+{{TEXT}}
+</text>
+```
+
+**Translate**
+
+```
+Translate the text between <text> tags into English.
+Output the translation only, with no original text and no notes.
+
+<text>
+{{TEXT}}
+</text>
+```
+
+**Rewrite tone**
+
+```
+Rewrite the text between <text> tags to sound more formal and concise.
+Keep the meaning identical. Output only the rewritten text.
+
+<text>
+{{TEXT}}
+</text>
+```
+
+---
+
+## 9. Always verify
+
+Treat `answer` as **untrusted text**. Validate or re-check anything
+safety-critical before you use it — web AIs hallucinate, and this tool returns
+whatever the page produced.
