+### Attaching a file (image, PDF, ...)
+
+```bash
+ask-web-ai ask "Transcribe the text in this image, then explain what it is for." \
+  -p deepseek --attach ./photo.png --json
+```
+
+`--attach <path>` is repeatable (`-a` for short). The tool only *hands* the file to
+the site; whether the site accepts it depends on the account — a signed-out
+session usually rejects uploads, in which case you get a clear
+`attachment_failed` result (never a silent empty answer). Run
+`login --provider <id>` once for a site you actually have an account on, then
+attach freely.
+
+> OCR / vision needs a provider with image support. Use a signed-in provider
+> (deepseek, qwen, chatgpt, gemini) — `duckai` is text-only and declares no
+> attachment support on purpose.
+
